# 2. NON-NEGOTIABLE DEVELOPMENT REQUIREMENTS

1. Build a complete working application, not merely an architecture or plan.
2. Use Python as the primary programming language.
3. Build a browser-based web application only.
4. Do not build a desktop application.
5. Do not require React or TypeScript. Prefer Python server-rendered templates with HTML, CSS, JavaScript and HTMX where appropriate.
6. Use modular, maintainable and testable architecture.
7. Do not create placeholder pages for features that are supposed to work.
8. Never display fabricated backtest results, market data, trades or performance metrics.
9. Every dashboard metric must come from actual calculations or clearly identified sample data.
10. Every research experiment must be reproducible.
11. Preserve historical experiment results.
12. Implement proper database persistence.
13. Implement background processing for long-running research jobs.
14. Support restarting interrupted research jobs.
15. Handle API errors, missing data, exchange rate limits and database failures.
16. Never use future information when calculating historical signals.
17. Prevent look-ahead bias, survivorship bias and data leakage.
18. Never optimize strategies using the final untouched test dataset.
19. Include automated unit tests, integration tests and end-to-end tests.
20. Do not stop after creating the project structure.

You must implement, execute, inspect, debug and verify the complete application.

If a feature cannot be implemented because of an external API limitation, clearly document the limitation and implement the best available alternative. Never pretend that unsupported data is available.

